{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe project pins Opus 4.8, Sonnet 4.6 and Haiku 4.5 (`rebar.toml`, `.github/llm-providers/*.toml`). Bedrock (896586841071/us-east-1) serves the 5.5 inference profiles. The epic lands this first, on the current engine.\n\nA bare swap is unsafe: on 5.5 forced `tool_choice` and assistant prefill 400, Opus thinking cannot be disabled, sampling parameters 400, and Opus/Haiku default `effort` to `medium`. pydantic-ai-slim 1.107.9's profile does not list 5.5 ids.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Riskiest assumption first (measured).** rebar sends no forced tool choice, thinking toggle or prefill: `structured.output_mode` (`src/rebar/llm/structured.py:149`) returns only `NativeOutput` or `PromptedOutput`; `capabilities._REBAR_OVERRIDES` (`capabilities.py:214`) pins Claude to `PromptedOutput`; no caller sets `RunRequest.thinking=True` (`runner.py:93`). The wire behaviour was probed on 2026-11-09 with one short call per case on each 5.5 model, on Bedrock (boto3 `converse`) and direct Anthropic (SDK): a bare call is accepted, `temperature=0` is rejected (400 \"`temperature` is deprecated for this model\"), and `effort` (Bedrock `additionalModelRequestFields={\"output_config\": {\"effort\": ...}}`, direct `output_config.effort`) is accepted.\n\n**Ids and tables.** Replace 4.x ids with the 5.5 ids verbatim (direct `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `claude-haiku-5-5`; Bedrock `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5`). Taken verbatim from `list-inference-profiles` (2026-11-09); Haiku 5.5's has no dated suffix. They go in the three toml files, `config.DEFAULT_MODEL`/`VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`src/rebar/llm/config.py:61,67`), `model_classes.TRIVIAL_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`model_classes.py:45`), `bedrock_model.DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` and `provider_parity.CLASS_SLOTS`. An explicitly pinned 4.x model keeps working: `MODEL_WINDOW_LADDER` (`model_classes.py:62-66`) becomes the 5.5 escalation ladder (all 1M) and the 4.x windows move to `PRIOR_GENERATION_WINDOWS`, consulted before the 200K unlocated floor, so Sonnet 4.6 keeps 1M without cross-generation escalation; `review_kernel/verify.py::MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` gains 5.5 rows (128K) beside the 4.x rows. The deploy defaults in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:97-99` and the alarm `ModelId` dimensions in `infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf:80-135` change in the same commit, because `tests/unit/test_reviewbot_bedrock_cutover.py` requires the compose slots to equal `bedrock.toml` byte for byte and the alarms to watch exactly those ids. The post-deploy check that Bedrock publishes metrics under those ids is the sibling task `itchy-neutral-whooper`. `sizing._RUNG_CLASSES` (`plan_review/sizing.py:240`) keys on family substrings; no change.\n\n**Sampling.** Add each 5.5 id (bare, `us.`, `global.`) to `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` (`capabilities.py:223`) with `supports_temperature: False`, the mechanism already used for Opus 4.7/4.8, so `structured_run.build_model_settings` (`:400-404`) omits Pass-2 `temperature=0`.\n\n**Effort, explicit.** rebar sends no `effort` today (no `effort`/`output_config` key is set under `src/rebar/llm`), so Opus 4.8 and Sonnet 4.6 run at the API default, which the documented default `high`. To keep today's depth, a per-model table pins `high` for Opus and Sonnet 5.5; Haiku 4.5 had no effort parameter, so Haiku 5.5 keeps its default `medium`. `structured_run.build_model_settings` sends it (the `model_settings` every call receives, `runner.py:495-518`) through pydantic-ai 1.107.9's provider-scoped settings: `anthropic_effort` on direct Anthropic, which `AnthropicModel` copies into `output_config.effort` unconditionally (`pydantic_ai/models/anthropic.py:1960-1978`; the profile flag only gates the thinking-derived fallback), and `bedrock_additional_model_requests_fields={\"output_config\": {\"effort\": ...}}` on Bedrock (`pydantic_ai/models/bedrock.py:338`, merged at `:706`). No profile override is needed: rebar never requests a forced tool, and sampling is withdrawn by the override table above.\n\n**Cache minimum.** Add the three direct 5.5 ids to `_MODEL_CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` (`capabilities.py:38`) at 512.\n\n**Reasoning-in-output wording (found by the audit).** Bedrock Opus 5.5 declines (`content_filtered`) any request whose output schema asks for reasoning in the response: `analysis` described as \"Scratchpad — reason before emitting.\" (`plan_review/passes.py:72`, `code_review/contracts.py:75,93`) or \"REASON FIRST…\" (`review_kernel/verify_models.py:126`). Measured: plan-review-T10 and code-review-failover declined 3 of 3; with only that description neutral, both pass. The four descriptions become neutral notes; `tests/unit/test_output_contract_no_reasoning_in_output.py` scans every registered contract.\n\n**Audit.** Walk every model call site (runner, settings builders, provider construction, review kernel, passes, workflow) against the five changes plus the `refusal` stop reason, and record one row per check (site, finding, fix or \"not affected\") as a ticket comment. Anything needing more than these seams is filed as a bug linked `discovered_from`.\n\nThese seams already shape every call, so correcting them corrects every pass without touching the passes. The eval-spec `model:` pins move in the sibling task `real-pubescent-turnstone` (see links).\n\n## Scope\n\n- rebar.toml, .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml, .github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml\n- src/rebar/llm/config.py, model_classes.py, capabilities.py, structured_run.py, agent_call.py, bedrock_model.py\n- src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py, src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json\n- infra/compose/docker-compose.yml, infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf\n- tests: the five files a measured spike showed break (all edits applied, 220 test files that name a 4.x id, a changed constant, or a provider/compose/alarm file run: 24 failures in these five, 3,924 passes, including `test_reviewbot_bedrock_cutover.py`): tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py, test_model_classes.py, test_plan_review.py, test_provider_parity.py, test_verifier_class.py; plus new cases in tests/unit/test_capabilities.py and tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: each 5.5 id reports `supports_temperature=False` and a 512 cache minimum; a 5.5 Bedrock request carries `output_config.effort` and no `temperature`; a direct one carries `anthropic_effort`.\n- Edge: an unmapped id keeps family defaults; a pinned 4.x id keeps its window; `sizing` maps Haiku 5.5 to `trivial`.\n- Live: provider-parity probe and full run once on 4.x before the change and once on 5.5 after, `AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'claude-(opus-4-8|sonnet-4-6|haiku-4-5)' -- rebar.toml .github/llm-providers src/rebar/llm/config.py src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py infra/compose/docker-compose.yml infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf` prints nothing, and `TRIVIAL_DEFAULT_MODEL` is `\"claude-haiku-5-5\"` (the files where ids are replaced; the per-model tables keep their 4.x rows by design).\n- [ ] The model-call audit is a ticket comment with one row per call site and API change.\n- [ ] Every incompatibility the audit finds is fixed here or filed as a linked bug.\n- [ ] The capability and settings-builder tests under Testing pass.\n- [ ] A ticket comment records, for each 5.5 model on Bedrock and on direct Anthropic, that a bare call and a call with the pinned `effort` are accepted and a `temperature=0` call is rejected.\n- [ ] The before and after provider-parity results are recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] The 5.5 provider-parity run reports `invalid: false` for both slots.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_output_contract_no_reasoning_in_output.py` passes.\n- [ ] The after prompt-eval run (ticket comment) shows no `content_filter` run error on any plan-review or code-review spec.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794270686102174001,"uuid":"62039bf2-fdf9-4b72-856e-556d127c6504"}